DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       Solaris introduced routines to allow portable access to  the  internals
       of the _F_I_L_E structure, and glibc also implemented these.

       The ____ffbbuuffssiizzee() function returns the size of the buffer currently used
       by the given stream.

       The  ____ffppeennddiinngg() function returns the number of characters in the out‐
       put buffer.  For wide‐oriented streams the  unit  is  wide  characters.
       This  function is undefined on buffers in reading mode, or opened read‐
       only.

       The ____ffllbbff() function returns a nonzero value if the  stream  is  line‐
       buffered, and zero otherwise.

       The ____ffrreeaaddaabbllee() function returns a nonzero value if the stream allows
       reading, and zero otherwise.

       The ____ffwwrriittaabbllee() function returns a nonzero value if the stream allows
       writing, and zero otherwise.

       The  ____ffrreeaaddiinngg()  function  returns  a  nonzero value if the stream is
       read‐only, or if the last operation on the stream was a read operation,
       and zero otherwise.

       The ____ffwwrriittiinngg() function returns a nonzero  value  if  the  stream  is
       write‐only (or append‐only), or if the last operation on the stream was
       a write operation, and zero otherwise.

       The  ____ffsseettlloocckkiinngg() function can be used to select the desired type of
       locking on the stream.  It returns the current type.  The _t_y_p_e argument
       can take the following three values:

       FFSSEETTLLOOCCKKIINNGG__IINNTTEERRNNAALL
              Perform implicit locking around every  operation  on  the  given
              stream (except for the *_unlocked ones).  This is the default.

       FFSSEETTLLOOCCKKIINNGG__BBYYCCAALLLLEERR
              The  caller will take care of the locking (possibly using fflloocckk‐‐
              ffiillee(3) in case there is more than one thread),  and  the  stdio
              routines  will  not do locking until the state is reset to FFSSEETT‐‐
              LLOOCCKKIINNGG__IINNTTEERRNNAALL.

       FFSSEETTLLOOCCKKIINNGG__QQUUEERRYY
              Don’t change the type of locking.  (Only return it.)

       The __fflluusshhllbbff() function flushes all line‐buffered  streams.   (Presum‐
       ably  so  that  output  to a terminal is forced out, say before reading
       keyboard input.)

       The ____ffppuurrggee() function discards the contents of the stream’s buffer.

